      {
        "name": "Custom retry policy via StorageRetryOptions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Configures StorageRetryOptions with retryPolicyType: EXPONENTIAL, configurable maxRetries and maxRetryDelayInMs from environment variables."
      },
      {
        "name": "SDK logging via @azure/logger setLogLevel()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Calls setLogLevel() from @azure/logger with configurable level; also sets AzureLogger.log handler."
      },
      {
        "name": "Blob lease acquisition via BlobLeaseClient",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "acquireLease() gets BlobLeaseClient via blockBlobClient.getBlobLeaseClient(), acquires lease with configurable duration, passes leaseId in conditions for uploadWithLease."
      },
      {
        "name": "Uses BlockBlobClient.uploadStream() for streaming",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Both upload() and uploadWithLease() use blockBlobClient.uploadStream() with 4MB buffer size and 5 concurrent uploads. No uploadData() or full-buffer upload()."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets blob index tags on upload via tags property",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Tags passed as options.tags in BlockBlobUploadStreamOptions for both upload and uploadWithLease methods."
      },
      {
        "name": "Downloads blob via readableStreamBody",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "download() accesses downloadResponse.readableStreamBody and reads chunks via for-await-of over the Node.js Readable stream."
      },
      {
        "name": "Lists blobs using for await...of over listBlobsFlat()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "listBlobs() uses 'for await (const blob of iterator)' over containerClient.listBlobsFlat() result."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles lease conflict errors (409 status code)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No handling for 409 lease conflict errors. acquireLease and uploadWithLease have no error handling for already-leased blobs."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles blob not found errors (404 status code)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No handling for 404 errors on download or delete operations. Operations will throw unhandled RestError."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using uploadData()/upload() with full buffer",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Correctly uses uploadStream() with fs.createReadStream() — never buffers entire file in memory."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using connection strings or account keys",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential with endpoint URL. No connection strings, account keys, or SAS tokens anywhere."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT collecting all listed blobs into array before processing",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "listBlobs() collects all blobs into a BlobItem[] array via push before returning. The demo then iterates the array — blobs are not processed during streaming."
      }
    ]
  },
  "overall_score": 19,
  "max_score": 27,
  "summary": "The code is well-structured with good separation of concerns and correctly implements core blob operations using streaming uploads, lease management, and managed identity. However, it has significant gaps in error handling (no RestError/status code handling for 404 or 409), uses outdated package versions, is missing @azure/logger as an explicit dependency, and collects all listed blobs into an array rather than processing them during iteration.",
